inl note_of_test_signal_metrics_1 () = Note ("TEST-SIGNAL-METRICS", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:50Z", "main-thread", "08:50 cost shares re-measured on single-flight-20261014-073517 (4,094 jobs, 3.77 h of summed compile+native): Gleam 27.0% (129 rows, ~28 s each, a cold gleam build + run per row), Rust 13.4%, Swift 10.5%, Bend 10.2%, C 8.6%, Lean 8.0%, Delphi 5.5%, Zig 5.0%, F# 2.9% (compile only), Wgsl 2.4%. Kotlin left the top 10 since the warm Kotlin server (was 41%). Next levers: Gleam pre-pass (lane B), Swift batching (SWIFT-WARM-COMPILE, main), then the composite-program compaction of the nested families.")
inl note_of_test_signal_metrics_2 () = Note ("TEST-SIGNAL-METRICS", 2u32, "2026-10-14T15:48Z", "lane-b", "Gleam pre-pass in test.ps1 (lane B, uncommitted): every Gleam row is a module of one project, one gleam build (128 of 129 in 21 s), lanes run erl -noshell -pa <ebins>; -Backend C,Gleam -Suite examples run single-flight-20261014-113713: 128 ran, all agree with C, exit+stdout identical to oracle run 095423, baseline 630 parity / 0 regressed; Gleam native median 2.9 s vs 10.1 s (sum 466 s vs 1,449 s)")
inl note_of_test_signal_metrics_3 () = Note ("TEST-SIGNAL-METRICS", 3u32, "2026-10-14T15:48Z", "main-thread", "11:48 both top cost levers landed in test.ps1: Gleam one-project pre-pass (lane B; per-row median 10.1 -> 2.9 s, sum 1,449 -> 466 s, 128/128 agree, single-flight-20261014-113713) and Swift 16-program chunks (main; C+Swift native tier 547 -> 314 s, 248/248 agree, single-flight-20261014-110801). Gleam was 27% and Swift 10.5% of the suite's summed cost. Next: measure a full suite's wall time with both.")
inl note_of_test_signal_metrics_4 () = Note ("TEST-SIGNAL-METRICS", 4u32, "2026-10-15T10:49Z", "main-thread", "06:49 groom: both cost levers are in test.ps1 (Gleam one-project pre-pass, Swift chunks; committed 570be6a6), and fast-tier.ps1 is documented in tmp/AGENTS.md. Full suites tonight took 21-23 min on 3 workers. Done.")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_1 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:31Z", "main-thread", "08:31 blast radius: !!!!StringLength/StringIndex/StringSlice appear in 0 lib .spi (spiral, polyglot) and only apps/compiler/tmp/tests/rust-exports (ASCII), so byte semantics only affect samples. Codegen: both F# copies (spiral_compiler.fs ~165250/165386/165409 and ~166425/166560/166583) share one length helper for arrays and strings; plan: a stringLength arm using System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetByteCount, index via GetBytes(s).[i] as char, slice via GetString(bytes, from, upto-from+1) with the Delphi-style continuation/bounds exit 3. Next: patch both sides in the next pack, then an F# native tier (dotnet fsi) in test.ps1.")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_2 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 2u32, "2026-10-14T12:42Z", "main-thread", "08:42 implemented in source (both core sides): StringLength -> UTF8.GetByteCount, StringIndex/StringSlice -> helpers emitted once via global' (slice exits 3 on bad bounds or a cut UTF-8 sequence, like Delphi/Lean). Array length output unchanged. Hand-built .fsx of samples/string_utf8 under dotnet fsi: exit 1 before, 0 after (= C). Lands with the next pack build; the F# native tier is still open. Char stays the unsigned byte (C sign-extends), which only matters if a char is converted to an int.")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_3 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 3u32, "2026-10-14T18:24Z", "main-thread", "14:24 F# UTF-8 length/index/slice installed with pack-1d (string_utf8, string_eq and multiline_triple_string F# residuals changed and were blessed in single-flight-20261014-140125). Left: an F# native tier in test.ps1.")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_4 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 4u32, "2026-10-15T10:48Z", "main-thread", "06:48 groom: F# rows still have no native tier (960 rows, 0 native). A cheap tier exists now: tonight's tmp/fsbase builds a Release exe per program from main.fsx via a one-file fsproj (11-21 s per build, runs at C-like speed). Next grain: wire that into test.ps1 as an F# native lane in chunks, like Swift.")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_5 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 5u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: F# rows can now be run natively (FSHARP-NATIVE-TIER prototype): of 329 F# rows with a C row, 327 agree in exit and stdout (string_utf8 included) and 2 fail to compile in fsi (FSHARP-MACRO-MUTATION); none differ.")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_6 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 6u32, "2026-10-18T16:10Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 12:10 main-thread, re-checked against today's native F# tier. Review 5 (single-flight-20261018-084525) ran all 976 F# rows natively, and every one of the 330 that has a C row matches C on exit and stdout, including samples/string_utf8 (exit 0; it exited 1 under fsi on 10-12) and string_eq. The managed UTF-8 samples have no F# row yet, so I probed them by hand with the tier's fsi exit wrap: managed_string_utf8_boundaries F# exit 0 (C 0) and managed_string_invalid_utf8_slice F# exit 3 (C 3). So F# has C's byte semantics for length, index and slice, and the item's other request (an F# native tier) landed today (FSHARP-NATIVE-TIER). Left, after today's accept (adding rows before it would break the row-for-row reproduction): add both samples to the Fsharp list in tests/matrix.psd1, then close.")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_7 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 7u32, "2026-10-19T12:34Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:34 lap 1 grain: today's pack 5 review: F# 980 rows, 334 agree with C, 0 disagree, 1 known, 214 no-c (F#-only samples), 431 contract rows without an oracle; the 5 percent left is the managed UTF-8 samples having no F# row (note 6 probed them by hand) Next: add the managed_string_* samples to the matrix F# list and let the next review score them against C")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_8 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 8u32, "2026-10-19T13:31Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:31 lap 2 grain: the last 5 percent is wired. F# membership comes from the Backends groups in tests/matrix.psd1; 13 managed_string samples (array, builder, codepoints, concat, empty_slice, index, record, recursive, runtime, runtime_choice, shared_calls, slice, union) sat in the C,Rust,Delphi group, while invalid_utf8_slice and utf8_boundaries were already in Fsharp,C,Rust,Delphi (today's review has F# rows for exactly those 2). Moved the 13 into the Fsharp,C,Rust,Delphi group with lab/FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS/move-managed-strings.py (anchored, dry run first; the data file loads, the group now holds all 15). Effect: the next matrix review adds 13 new F# rows scored natively against C; they need that review plus an accept (main's runs). Next: read those 13 rows in the next review; if all agree with C, Done")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_9 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 9u32, "2026-10-19T13:54Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:54 DONE with evidence: main's review-keys round B (spiral-bin/runs/single-flight-20261019-094419/results.tsv) ran the 13 managed_string samples moved into the Fsharp,C,Rust,Delphi group natively on F#; all 15 managed_string F# rows score oracle agree with C (Group-Object over that results.tsv: agree 15, nothing else). With string_utf8, string_eq and the 2 earlier utf8 rows, F# UTF-8 length/index/slice now match C on every managed string sample in the matrix. The rows enter the oracle with the next accept")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_10 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 10u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 3 09:54 (subagent2): DONE: round B single-flight-20261019-094419 has all 15 managed_string F# rows agree with C -> next: -")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_1 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 1u32, "2026-10-14T10:54Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-14 06:54 blocked on the user's commit and push: nothing committed since 23:49 (spiral 401, eoie 49 uncommitted entries); the fixes (kino rustup lock, alphabet font, near_wallet) are in the tree")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_2 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 2u32, "2026-10-14T10:59Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-14 06:59 review: verified on GitHub (i574n remotes; gh's default repo is the fc1943s fork with 2025 runs): i574n/spiral d94dc380 failure, eoie 4d8935e failure (ubuntu native ok, windows failure), i574n.github 5a49dde failure, i574n/alphabet 3a1f1c3 failure, i574n/dice 923ca84 failure, i574n/polyglot b61d381c success; every fix is in the uncommitted tree")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_3 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 3u32, "2026-10-14T12:46Z", "main-thread", "08:46 CI on the 07:25 pushes: polyglot green (1h03), eoie red (planning_cli notes order; lane B fix ready, 1 line), spiral red, dice red, alphabet red. spiral: lib/spiral test blocks fail in 20 files (parsing 17, sm' 23, base, date_time, ...). The cause in every 'targets disagree' line: the cuda target's output starts with CuPy's 'UserWarning: CUDA path could not be detected' (the runner has no CUDA), while the assertion lines match gleam's. Fix: PYTHONWARNINGS=ignore:CUDA path could not be detected:UserWarning on the cuda run, or drop that warning when comparing (Kino, lane B). dice: contract/dice_contract.spi 7/7 tests fail with 'spiral rust --rs-path ... --contract=' exit 1 (spiral.process_rust wasm error); the cargo stderr is not in the log. Next: surface it, then reproduce locally.")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_4 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 4u32, "2026-10-14T12:46Z", "main-thread", "08:46 alphabet run 38556512728: ubuntu-24.04 green (1h08); windows-2025 died after 1h11 with 'hosted runner lost communication', so no test failed (the runner was starved or killed; logs are gone). Its Windows lib job mirrors dice's (alphabet mirrors dice), so expect the dice contract failure there too once it runs to the end. Diagnosis for spiral and dice sent to lane B (Kino).")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_5 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 5u32, "2026-10-14T13:10Z", "lane-b", "lane B, dice 38556488193 (windows only, ubuntu green): not Kino dropping stderr; apps/spiral/spiral.spi process_rust runs the contract's spiral_wasm through invoke-block.ps1 -Linux, which on the Windows runner is bash: 'workspace/target/release/spiral_wasm: No such file or directory' (exit 127, printed by Invoke-Block, not captured into spiral_wasm_result); fix belongs in spiral.spi: use the native spiral_wasm.exe on Windows, and append its output to the error")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_6 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 6u32, "2026-10-14T13:21Z", "lane-b", "lane B, spiral 38556487627 CuPy fix (uncommitted, apps/kino targets.ex + targets_test.exs): every python/cuda/spiral target process gets PYTHONWARNINGS += ignore:CUDA path could not be detected:UserWarning (keeps existing filters); test runs real python with that warning: 18/18 in a clean copy, red without the fix; dice: -Linux = wsl bash, so WSL lacks the Linux spiral_wasm")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_7 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 7u32, "2026-10-14T13:22Z", "main-thread", "09:22 decision (main): the dice/alphabet Windows contract failure is spiral.spi process_rust running spiral_wasm via invoke-block -Linux (the NEAR sandbox is Linux-only). On the Windows runner WSL has no workspace/target/release/spiral_wasm (exit 127). Fix direction: the Windows CI job builds spiral_wasm inside WSL before the contract step, with no skip switch and no native-Windows contract path, and process_rust captures invoke-block's output into spiral_wasm_result so the next failure names its cause. Per the WSL rule it lands last, after the rest of the workflow is green. The CuPy fix (lane B, Kino targets.ex) is ready to commit.")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_8 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 8u32, "2026-10-14T17:56Z", "lane-b", "lane B pack corpus check (job tmp lane-b/sweep-*): pack-1b lib 38 notebooks 319 passed / 10 failed, all 10 the Python slice pair (sm'.slice to_py +1 vs inclusive StringSlice); pack-1d with the patched sm': all green (9 notebooks + runtime rerun 7/7), baseline deployed 88/0, Tibia hunt_sim 11/11 gpu_sim 6/6 equal on both DLLs")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_9 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 9u32, "2026-10-14T20:42Z", "lane-b", "pack-1e corpus check (lane B): lib 38/38 notebooks, 329 tests, 0 failed; Tibia hunt_sim 11/11 + gpu_sim 6/6 with the chunking spiral-wgsl; 0 ETY-UnionCaseAmbiguous hits; Kino suite on the tree-equivalent copy 229/229")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_10 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 10u32, "2026-10-14T21:22Z", "main-thread", "17:22 status: spiral's CI blocker (the CuPy warning in cuda target output) is fixed in Kino (lane B, uncommitted); eoie's planning_cli fix is uncommitted; dice's Windows contract needs spiral_wasm built inside WSL (decided; lands last per the WSL rule). Stays Blocked on the user's commit and the next CI run.")
