inl note_of_source_boundary_authority_1 () = Note ("SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY", 1u32, "2026-10-14T13:09Z", "lane-b", "host --test-blocks <file> (name, header row, body first/last row, header text from wdiff_tokenizer_all + blocks) proven in a scratch host build: edge suite 10/10 equal to the overnight fsx probe; patch for main: job tmp/lane-b/patches/malformed-test-header.ps1 (MalformedTestHeader parse error; same grammar over the 583-file corpus: 425/430 headers valid, the 5 rejects are exactly the edge cases)")
inl note_of_source_boundary_authority_2 () = Note ("SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY", 2u32, "2026-10-14T13:09Z", "lane-b", "correction to note 1: with the patch's grammar (no body check) the corpus gives 426/430 valid; rejects: test c (no =), test b = 1, test<TAB>d, unknown flag; 'test i=' is accepted (tokens ignore spacing) while Kino's header_of rejects it")
inl note_of_source_boundary_authority_3 () = Note ("SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY", 3u32, "2026-10-14T13:55Z", "lane-b", "Kino side landed (uncommitted): Document.parse_spi(spi, spir, {bounds, bounds}) keeps every row up to the compiler body_last, so col-0 continuations of a triple-quoted string or a block comment stay in the test (document_test). Host (scratch build, lands after main's pack): --test-blocks IN OUT|-, --capabilities, test-blocks over --server-tcp; edge suite 10/10 equal")
