inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_1 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:09Z", "lane-b", "status 2026-10-14: still blocked on the tibia lane's exact failing command; apps/tibia/package.spiproj still uses the hunting_pack workaround; no new repro reported since 10-13 09:55")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_2 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 2u32, "2026-10-15T10:48Z", "main-thread", "06:48 groom: still blocked on an exact failing command from the Tibia session (not reproduced in any Kino suite since: tree suite 236 tests on pack-1g). Lowered P2 -> P3 until a repro arrives.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_3 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 3u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night repro attempt on tonight Kino (package outside the tree, modules pack_sim then pack, open pack and pack.troll): passes with memo off and on (second run 2 hits). Still blocked on the Tibia session exact command.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_4 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 4u32, "2026-10-19T12:43Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:43 helper-lane lap 1: turned the blocker (waiting for the tibia lane's exact command) into a self-serve check: tibia/src/package.spiproj still carries the workaround (module hunting_pack, 5 qualified uses; pack_sim.spi is the notebook stem), and every synthetic repro since 10-13 passed. lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/run.ps1 copies tibia/src's .spi/.spiproj into a cache probe dir named src, renames hunting_pack back to pack (file and every mention), runs Cells on pack_sim.spi exactly like the blog/x runners (process compiler, no warm), and counts UnboundModule lines; the tibia tree itself is only read. HEAVY QUEUE: C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab\\KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND\\run.ps1 (~15 min). 0 UnboundModule means the bug is gone on the real tree and the item can close; a hit gives the exact failing state.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_5 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 5u32, "2026-10-19T13:28Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:28 helper-lane lap 2: reviewed the existing regression test (notebook_report_test.exs:640, a package module named like a prefix of the notebook's stem stays in the test program): it runs with a stub compile function and only asserts that the generated program text contains open pack, so it cannot see a compiler-side resolution failure (ETY-UnboundModule comes from the real compiler resolving the package's module list, where the 10-13 case had pack listed last). That is why the real-compiler probe queued in lap 1 (lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/run.ps1 on a renamed copy of tibia/src) is the meaningful check, and why the stub test passing since 10-13 never settled the item.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_6 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 6u32, "2026-10-19T14:25Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:25 main heavy queue: run.ps1 threw before probing (Join-Path on an empty Split-Path for a top-level src file); fixed line 7 in the lab script (top-level hunting_pack.spi maps to pack.spi) and requeued in main's queue 2.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_7 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 7u32, "2026-10-19T14:49Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:49 main heavy queue 2 ran the fixed run.ps1 (10:45-10:46): the 10-13 bug still reproduces on a renamed copy of the real tibia tree: probes/prefix-module-20261019-1045/src/pack_sim.spi:3:10 ETY-UnboundModule (plus a follow-on _assert_eq unbound at 16:88), UnboundModule lines 1; so the item stays Blocked on a Cells or compiler fix for a package module whose name is a prefix of another (pack vs pack_sim).")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_8 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 8u32, "2026-10-19T15:08Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 11:08 helper-lane lap 3: the 10:49 reproduction is not evidence for the prefix bug: run.ps1 now takes -Control (copy without the hunting_pack -> pack rename), and the control copy in the same cache probes folder fails IDENTICALLY (lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/run-control-20261019-1104.log: pack_sim.spi:3:10 ETY-UnboundModule on the static prelude's open testing, then _assert_eq unbound at 16:88; 24 of 31 tests failed). open testing resolves through the spiral lib package Cells mounts for the tree, and a copy under spiral-bin/probes cannot reach it, so the unbound module is the probe's location, not the module name. run.ps1 also takes -InTree (copy under the lab folder, where lib resolves); an in-tree control started compiling for real and passed the 150 s bound (pack_sim declares --timeout 1800000), so both in-tree variants go to the heavy queue. Status back to Active: blocked only on that measurement, not on a fix.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_9 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 9u32, "2026-10-19T15:09Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 11:09 correction to main's note 7: that run does not show the prefix bug; helper lane 1's control (same copy without the rename, run-control-20261019-1104.log) fails identically, because a copy under spiral-bin/probes cannot reach the spiral lib package (open testing unbound). The in-tree pair (-InTree, with and without -Control) after the switch accept is the real test.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_10 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 10u32, "2026-10-19T15:37Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 11:37 helper-lane lap 4: found the Cells-side guard already in the tree: notebook_report_test.exs line 700 (a package module named like a prefix of the notebook's stem stays in the test program, committed in 59b477ba on 10-17) builds exactly the reported shape - package module pack, notebook pack_sim.spi with a static prelude opening testing and a test that opens pack - and asserts the generated test program keeps the line open pack and passes. That covers the Cells text path with a stubbed compiler; what is left unproven is only the real-compiler run, which the queued in-tree pair (run.ps1 -InTree and -InTree -Control) decides. If both in-tree runs pass, the item closes as fixed by 59b477ba plus that evidence.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_11 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 11u32, "2026-10-19T21:54Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 17:54 helper-lane: the in-tree pair (lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/run.ps1 -InTree, with lib reachable, on the installed pack 10 compiler) reproduces the bug with the real compiler. The copy with hunting_pack renamed to pack fails 22 of 31 tests on c with main.spi:5:6 ETY-UnboundModule in open pack (run-20261019-1742.log). The unrenamed control passes 31 of 31 (run-control-20261019-1745.log). So 59b477ba's stubbed Cells test does not cover it: the text keeps open pack, but the module is still unbound at compile time. Next: separate prefix from name with a minimal package (module pack plus a notebook named other.spi, and the same with pack_sim.spi), to tell a stem-prefix filter from a clash with the name pack.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_12 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 12u32, "2026-10-19T22:06Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 18:06 helper-lane lap 6: narrowed to a cross-cell effect of a Rust target. It is not the module name and not the stem prefix alone. Minimal packages (module pack with notebooks other.spi and pack_sim.spi, with and without a type pack, and with a rust+c cell between two c cells) all pass. On the real tibia package with hunting_pack renamed to pack: current_first_targeting alone on c passes; after cyclops_hits (c only) it passes; after golden_seed_7_troll_pack (///> rust + ///> c, both pass) it fails with main.spi:5:6 ETY-UnboundModule open pack (prefix-two, 1 of 2). In the full run, every c test after that rust cell fails the same way. The cell dirs are fresh tmp dirs, the src dir gains no files, and the failing c compile is faster (8 s vs 15 s), so some cache shared across cells after a Rust compile of this package drops module pack, while hunting_pack survives. Repro: lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/one-run.ps1, which rebuilds the copies via make-variants.ps1 (copies removed after each run). Next: find the cache, either the compiler's package cache keyed by path or a mount reused by the rust patch step, by diffing spiral-bin cache dirs before and after the rust cell.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_13 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 13u32, "2026-10-19T22:10Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 18:10 helper-lane: correction to the 18:06 note. The Rust target is not involved. lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/one-run.ps1 -Only prefix-two-c -NoMemo (golden_seed_7 with only ///> c, then current_first_targeting, Cells memo off) still fails the second test with main.spi:5:6 open pack unbound. prefix-two fails the same way with the memo off, so the compile memo is ruled out. prefix-one (current_first alone) passes, and so does prefix-c-two (cyclops_hits, which only uses pack qualified, then current_first). So the trigger is a previous cell in the same notebook run that also opens pack. The minimal packages with two c cells that both open pack do not reproduce, so it also needs something in the tibia package (27 modules, or a module or term that the earlier cell's program pulls in). Next: capture the failing cell's generated main.spi (keep the cell tmp dir), and bisect the tibia package's modules list.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_14 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 14u32, "2026-10-19T22:35Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 18:35 helper-lane: ROOT CAUSE found; the module-name prefix was a red herring. I captured the cell programs with lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/keep-notebook.ps1 plus keep.exs, which run Notebook.run_report with keep_files: true. The failing program begins with open pack and open creatures copied from the previous test's body, ahead of the static prelude and the test's own open pack. Two things combine. (1) Cells: apps/cells/spi/notebook.spi line 263, the test = 1 branch of walk, merges a test cell's opens (cell_opens) into the opens of every later program (since feb8b9f7, 10-12), so a test's local open leaks into all later tests. (2) Compiler: tibia's module pack defines type pack, and after one open pack the second open pack resolves pack to the opened type rather than the module, which gives ETY-UnboundModule. hunting_pack never collided, which is why the rename fixed it. Minimal repro without tibia: lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/minimal/g_typed_twice (module pack with type pack, two c tests that each open pack): second_open fails with unbound=1, while h_plain_twice (no type pack) passes 2 of 2 (minimal-run.ps1). Fix staged: lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/test_opens_patch.py (apps/cells, --apply gated, dry run OK) keeps test opens local: the test body already carries them through scoped_test_body, and prelude opens still flow through the static defs branch. It goes to lane 2 via main, with g_typed_twice as the regression case. The compiler half, a module and a type sharing a name across open, stays a separate small item if wanted.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_15 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 15u32, "2026-10-20T00:24Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 20:24 helper-lane: the Cells fix is in the tree (uncommitted). In a Cells idle window I applied lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/test_opens_patch.py: apps/cells/spi/notebook.spi line 263, where a test cell's opens no longer merge into later programs. Before keeping it, mix test with the patch (cells-window-20261019-1946.log, per-run MIX_BUILD_PATH) ran notebook_report_test, notebook_targets_test and the new crates case: 36 passed. The runner misread the new ExUnit summary format (Result: 36 passed) as a failure and reverted once; it was re-applied by hand at about 20:10 and the check is fixed. On the patched Cells, the minimal repro passes (minimal-run.ps1 at about 20:25): g_typed_twice is now 2 of 2, where second_open failed with ETY-UnboundModule before, and h_plain_twice is 2 of 2. The tibia prefix-two case and the lib gates for testing, conversation and reactors are queued (after-patch-gates.ps1); Done once those pass.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_16 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 16u32, "2026-10-20T00:35Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 20:35 helper-lane: Done. On the patched Cells (test opens stay local; apps/cells/spi/notebook.spi line 263, uncommitted, for the user's commit), lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/after-patch-gates.ps1 passes the original tibia case: the tibia package with hunting_pack renamed back to pack runs golden_seed_7 then current_first_targeting, 2 of 2, unbound 0, where the second failed with ETY-UnboundModule open pack before. The minimal repro g_typed_twice is 2 of 2. No regression in the lib gates run on the patched Cells: testing 7 of 7, conversation 2 of 2, reactors 8 of 8. mix test was 36 passed. Cause recap: Cells leaked each test's open lines into every later test program, and tibia's module pack defines type pack, so a repeated open pack resolved to the type. The compiler side (a module and a same-named type colliding on a second open in one program) is not hit by Cells anymore; it can be filed separately if it matters in hand-written code.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_17 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 17u32, "2026-10-22T03:36Z", "main", "23:36 lab drain: the fix lives in apps/cells/spi/notebook.spi (now line 328 after reformatting: elif test = 1i32 then walk ... opens ... unchanged, no merge opens cell_opens site left; staged by the user). The folder held the patch script, Cells window logs and the two minimal repros (g_typed_twice, h_plain_twice); their outcomes (2 of 2, unbound 0, 36 passed) are in the notes above. Removed spiral/lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND (33 files).")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_18 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 18u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 5 12:19 (subagent): in-tree pair queued -> next: read the pair; close if equal | lap 7 18:35 (subagent): root cause: notebook.spi:263 leaks test opens + type pack shadows module pack; minimal repro g_typed_twice; fix staged -> next: lane 2 applies test_opens_patch.py, rerun minimal + tibia pair | lap 8 20:35 (subagent): Done: Cells test_opens fix in tree; tibia case 2/2, minimal 2/2, lib gates 7/2/8, mix 36 -> next: -")
inl note_of_spiral_record_update_expr_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-RECORD-UPDATE-EXPR", 1u32, "2026-10-14T11:59Z", "lane-a", "07:59 lane-a: patch ready, lane-a\\patches\\record-update-expr.ps1 (record_with base: var or rounds next; 2 anchors, dry-run ok on core 71184C99). Repro lane-a\\repro\\record_update_expr (expect exit 42). Needs main build+ladder.")
inl note_of_spiral_record_update_expr_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-RECORD-UPDATE-EXPR", 2u32, "2026-10-14T15:16Z", "lane-a", "11:16 lane-a: patch verified on an isolated Debug build (current core BFB7B6A3 + patch, 252 s): repro {(origin ()) with x = 40} fails on the 04:35 core ('Expected: lowercase variable'), compiles on the patched one, C run exits 42. Ready for main's pack.")
inl note_of_spiral_record_update_expr_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-RECORD-UPDATE-EXPR", 3u32, "2026-10-14T21:09Z", "lane-a", "Installed in pack-1e (patch record-update-expr.ps1, verified: {(e) with ...} compiles, repro exit 42; review 0 diffs).")
inl note_of_spiral_record_update_expr_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-RECORD-UPDATE-EXPR", 4u32, "2026-10-15T10:48Z", "main-thread", "06:48 groom: installed since pack-1e and carried by every pack since (1f-1h blesses, DISAGREE 0); the repro compiles with exit 42. Done; it gets no regression sample because it is a feature, not a bug fix.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: reproduced live a second time: PC-3 run 3 (arena-logs/20261015-063232-cyclops-spiral-retreat-3.log) retreated 23 times with 0 kills in 200 s. About 2 failures in about 70 retreat runs since v6. Raised to P2: it is a bug in the policy we race against the baselines.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 2u32, "2026-10-15T12:58Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 08:58 the 2026-10-15 occurrence (arena-logs/20261015-063232-cyclops-spiral-retreat-3.log) is not target spread: the knight retreated 23 times down the corridor south-east to 1940,1373 (about 24 tiles from the spot) by t=40 s, then saw no monster inside the 15x11 parity view and held for the remaining 160 s (holds 803, attacking nothing, 0 kills). The policy has no rule for 'nothing visible': it neither walks back nor seeks. Fix candidate (policy + probe + simulator together): when no monster is visible, walk back toward the spot (or the last seen monster); in the simulator, check whether live_retreat_tactic ever loses every monster under mirroring_the_live_arena and pin the rate.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 3u32, "2026-10-15T13:09Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 09:09 the simulator never reproduces it: under mirroring_the_live_arena, 0 of 300 training clears with live_retreat_tactic 160 2 exceed 200 s or end with the knight 15+ tiles from the spot (slowest 122 s). Live, the knight (about 450 ms per step) outran cyclopes (650-700 ms) down the corridor until they dropped it. Next: compare the simulator's monster sight (11 tiles both axes) and target-drop rule with Canary's (monster viewport and Monster::onCreatureLeave / target loss), then add a 'nothing visible: walk back' rule to the policy in both places.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 4u32, "2026-10-15T13:52Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 09:52 ROOT CAUSE: the failed run changed floor. Its last retreat step went from 1939,1371,7 by 1,1 onto 1940,1372 and the knight ended at 1940,1373,6; Canary's Monster::isTarget requires the same floor, so every cyclops dropped it, and the 15x11 view on floor 6 showed nothing. Only this run of all arena logs ever reached floor 6. otbm-walkability.py gained --items-xml/--floor-changes (items.xml floorchange ids, 997): floor-change tiles within radius 30 of the spot are 1927,1337, 1940,1371, 1941,1371 (stairs down); the climb at 1940,1372 comes from tile elevation, not floorchange. Fix after PR-9 (the probe is shared with spiral-policy, and suites wait for the live block): the probe's stepAway skips tiles with hasFloorChange() or hasElevation(3); the simulator blocks those tiles on ArenaSpot (monsters never take stairs either), then re-pin.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 5u32, "2026-10-15T14:10Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 10:10 correction to note 4: my items.xml parser let self-closing <item/> tags swallow the next block. Fixed; the floor-change tiles within radius 30 of the spot on floor 7 are 1927,1337, 1940,1372, 1941,1372 and 1958,1345 (tibia-local/arena-floor-changes.txt). 1940,1372 is the ramp (item 6913, floorchange south) the knight stepped onto; a floorchange-direction ramp moves the walker one floor up and one tile on, here to 1940,1373,6. No elevation climb involved (no tile with three height items in the region). Probe fix stays: skip tiles with hasFloorChange().")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 6u32, "2026-10-15T22:40Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:40 probe-policy-body.lua and probe-policy-diag-body.lua now skip tiles with hasFloorChange() in stepAway (applied after PR-9); arena masks block the four floor-change tiles; pack_sim/terrain re-pinned and gated 12:53 (79/79). Not yet verified live (no retreat block since).")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 7u32, "2026-10-15T22:51Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:51 the hand-edited arena masks are now reproducible: otbm-walkability.py --masks folds items.xml floorchange tiles in when --items-xml is given. At the simulator's center (--x 1933 --y 1350, sim 100,100 = server 1933,1350) all 61 rows match terrain.spi exactly with exits, and the pre-edit backup exactly without them.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 8u32, "2026-10-15T23:33Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 19:33 live harness check (5 spiral-retreat runs, arena-results-cyclops-harness-check-1015.tsv, not analyzed for potions): 5/5 cleared, 0 foreign actions, no floor-6 position in any log, one run retreated 46 steps and still cleared; the protection now ends at login for the retreat probe too (2-9 hits in the first 10 s). Floor-change fix exercised live; the rare failure itself needs many more runs to show absence.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 9u32, "2026-10-20T05:55Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-20 01:55 main (coordination, WSJF): tibia asked for three 57-min live chunks of PR-12 (retreat vs nExBot, 30 pre-registered pairs) from 01:55; slid to 07:00 or an earlier go from main, because the retreat line is P2 and the heavy gate is held by P0 work until about 06:45 (SEFAZ-XSD gates, the FORMATTER-DESTRUCTIVE-RUN matrix review, HOPACSOTA helpers' G3 suites) and live chunks need a quiet machine.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 10u32, "2026-10-20T11:13Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 07:13 ROOT CAUSE of the remaining failures: protection zone. PR-12 chunk 2 spiral-retreat run 10 (arena-logs/20261020-070211-cyclops-spiral-retreat-10.log) retreated onto 1943,1351 by t+28 s and stood there for 120 s: 404 'This action is not permitted in a protection zone' texts, 0 kills. The same signature is in exactly three older logs, all 0-kill no-clears stuck at 1942-1943,1350-1351: 20261013-194904 run 7 (the run that opened this item as 'target spread'), 20261014-091929 run 20, 20261014-095144 run 3. Floor change (10-15) and PZ are the two causes found; no failure is left that is target spread. Canary: monsters cannot enter PZ tiles and players cannot attack from them. apps/map now reads the OTBM tile-flag PZ bit and lists PZ and house tiles (run after the live block). Fix after PR-12 (the policy is frozen for it): retreat never steps onto a PZ tile (probe and simulator together), and the simulator blocks PZ tiles.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 11u32, "2026-10-20T11:26Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 07:25 apps/map reads the PZ flag: 420 PZ tiles within radius 45 (276 walkable), 48 row spans in two buildings, small x 1940-1947 y 1340-1351 (open at its south row, where the knight walks in) and large x 1954-1978 y 1321-1355 (open on its west). The map tool now emits arena_protection_zone dx dy as row spans (no bit ops, so C, WGSL and Lua can share it). Plan after PR-12 chunk 4 (src and apps/arena are read by every live run): terrain gains the generated function and a walk-only predicate (PZ blocks walking, not arrows' sight lines); monster and knight movement in the model use it; the live retreat treats PZ tiles as blocked; re-pin, gate, then a 5-run live harness check like 10-15. lab/tibia-retreat-target-spread/pz-overlay.ps1 draws the overlay.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_12 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 12u32, "2026-10-20T11:52Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 07:52 tally over all 239 live spiral-retreat cyclops logs (2026-10-13 to 10-20): 5 ended with 0 kills, all explained: 4 protection-zone traps (the only 4 logs of any competitor with PZ refusals) and 1 floor change (10-15, fixed). Staged fix compiles to Lua (lab/tibia-retreat-target-spread/staged, staged-check.ps1): terrain.arena_protection_zone generated by apps/map, terrain.walls (sight) vs terrain.blocked (walls + PZ at both arena layouts), hunting_pack arrows use walls, competitor.step_away treats PZ tiles as Blocked and labels them 'zone' in cornered reports. Applies after PR-12 chunk 4. Saved model hunter traces never touch a PZ tile, so PC-5 is expected to leave the hunter gap open.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_13 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 13u32, "2026-10-20T11:53Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 07:53 source check (canary src/items/tile.cpp:619, Tile::queryAdd): a monster's add is RETURNVALUE_NOTPOSSIBLE on any tile flagged TILESTATE_PROTECTIONZONE | TILESTATE_FLOORCHANGE | TILESTATE_TELEPORT (familiars excepted). PZ and floor change are now both modeled as monster walls; teleport tiles are not read by apps/map yet (follow-up: list teleport items within radius 45 and block them too if any exist). A player only fails to enter PZ when pz-locked (tile.cpp:738, PvP), which never happens in the arena.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_14 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 14u32, "2026-10-20T13:53Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 09:53 PZ fix applied to the tree (PR-12 complete): staged terrain.spi, hunting_pack.spi (arrows use walls), competitor.spi (retreat skips zone tiles) copied in; apps/map now also blocks teleport tiles (ids from items.xml value=teleport) and its build matches r45 and src/terrain.spi (3 generated definitions). Two terrain tests adjusted: the scan test now checks walls (walkability), and ArenaHunt spawn (124,96) = world 1957,1346 sat inside the east building's PZ, where Canary cannot place a monster; moved to the nearest legal tile (120,96) = 1953,1346. terrain 11/11 green. Next: pack_sim/hunt_sim/gpu_sim re-pins after the PC-4 slot, then PC-5 and the 5-run live harness check.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_15 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 15u32, "2026-10-20T13:55Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 09:55 PC-5 RESULT (pre-registered 07:26): hunter prediction on the tree with protection zones 87/100 clears (before 87), potions 2.10 (2.08), cleared 60.3 s (60.0), hits 14.8 (14.7). Above 80: the hunter gap (16/25 live) stays open and the zone is not its cause, as expected from the trace check. The change stays (server fact). lab/tibia-fidelity/hunter-prediction-r45-road-pz.txt.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_16 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 16u32, "2026-10-20T14:21Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 10:21 suites on the zone tree (SPIRAL_CELLS_JOBS=1): terrain 11/11, hunt_sim 11/11, gpu_sim 6/6 after one re-pin (hunting-ground hunt with routing, seed 1001: 21 kills/1330 exp -> 22/1350, potions 19, deaths 0; the ArenaHunt camp now routes around the east building's zone and spawns at 120,96). The GPU twin of that test passed before the re-pin too, which exposed WGSL-TEST-STATUS-IGNORED (Cells wgsl tests cannot fail); main took it at P1. pack_sim running.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_17 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 17u32, "2026-10-20T14:50Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 10:50 pack_sim 31/31 on the zone tree (first run reaped once by low memory, retried 10:25-10:43 at one job; 27/31, then the 4 failures run alone). Re-pinned 3 hunting-ground tests, every stated claim re-checked and still true: (1) ArenaHunt: tuned heal 100->120, standing 89020->104920, hand route 109700->108270, spawn loop 112470->114470, sweep 119760->119950, evolved shuttle 118810->119280 (walking pays, shuttle above both hand routes); (2) random control 46300->54310 exp, far below every rule; (3) six-cyclops ground: heals 110/190 -> 100/130, standing 121050 (0 deaths) -> 112700 (2), sweeping 138900 (0) -> 126900 (3) still leads, retreat+sweep 121050 at -166786 with 0 deaths (5% less exp for 44% lower cost). The 4th failure (kills_and_gold_do_not_add, a compile-error test) was a compiler-daemon :noproc under memory pressure and passes alone. README numbers updated (only those pinned by tests; 30 s respawn and two-knight figures are not pinned anywhere).")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_18 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 18u32, "2026-10-20T15:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 11:14 live harness check of the zone fix (5 spiral-retreat runs, PR-12 settings, 11:03-11:14, results/arena-results-cyclops-pz-check.tsv): 5/5 cleared, 0 deaths, no 'seen at' sample on a protection-zone tile (lab harness-check.ps1); lowest health 101/88/80/83/18 (run 5 came within one hit of death; descriptive, n=5). Combined with PC-5 (no model change) and suites green, the item's fix is complete; remaining: the teleport follow-up is folded in (apps/map blocks teleport ids). Ready for Done after the user commits.")
inl note_of_tibia_retreat_target_spread_19 () = Note ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", 19u32, "2026-10-21T09:12Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 05:12 Follow-up from the PR-16 analysis (TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY notes 82-85): live, the retreat-at-2 knight ends cornered in the pocket at 1936,1349 in 41 of 60 runs (south row 1935-1937,1350 and 1937,1348 blocked; a cyclops takes 1937,1349), and only 11 of 60 ever pass x 1945. The model escaped east in about half its clears until the overnight bundle (dance step, Canary step formula, tick-late view); now it takes 12.4 retreat steps per clear against 11.7 live. The live probe logs 'cornered' every tick it wants to step and cannot (cornered_report_every 50), so cornered counts are not comparable to the model's per-decision counter.")
inl note_of_eoie_table_query_1 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-QUERY", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:25Z", "lane-a", "08:25 lane-a: spec coverage map: cases 4,5,17,20,22,27 = 849 recorded calls, all 6 red (no table verb; nearest is none). Today's lane-A need: join two formatter listings by file:line (check vs space) went through pwsh Group-Object.")
inl note_of_eoie_table_query_2 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-QUERY", 2u32, "2026-10-15T10:50Z", "main-thread", "06:50 groom: evidence from tonight: the per-run comparisons (compare-runs.ps1 over results.tsv, per-backend group counts) were all ad-hoc Import-Csv pipelines. A table verb with group/diff over TSV would have replaced 6 scripts.")
inl note_of_eoie_table_query_3 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-QUERY", 3u32, "2026-10-17T18:23Z", "bundle-wisdom", "14:23 from the bundles (compiler alpha3006 agile_eoie.md, Sep 2026): every compiler diagnosis round needed jq/python for ordered JSONL causal queries: first/last/window/group plus joins by typed digest or job id, e.g. first terminal semantic failure -> owning method -> last normalization events for the same case -> run_end, with per-kind counts and a per-line JSON validity census (one invalid row came from a typed ref formatted with %u). Add this as a case shape. Also a typed TSV upsert (--key col=value --set col=value) with schema/cardinality validation: a shell wrapper once wrote a literal backslash-t into agile rows.")
inl note_of_eoie_table_query_4 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-QUERY", 4u32, "2026-10-17T20:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 16:28 needed on log corpora too, not only TSV: hundreds of run logs queried by time window and file-name pattern, a regex that turns matching lines into columns (value, timestamp), then group/mean/count per arm; today every such question was a fresh PowerShell loop.")
inl note_of_eoie_table_query_5 () = Note ("EOIE-TABLE-QUERY", 5u32, "2026-10-18T19:53Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 15:53 landed: crate eoie_table_query, table query <file> [--where col=value]... [--cols a,b] [--group col] [--limit n] and table diff <left> <right> --key a,b [--cols x,y] [--limit n] (TSV, CSV by extension); typed table_command union and table_request record built by option_applied steps, row engine as one host primitive; unknown columns are rejected with the header; e2e: group backend over 6994 rows in 63 ms, diff of review 110213 vs accept 123705 reproduces the main lane analysis (4 exit cells, 22 oracle cells, 4 new rows)")
inl note_of_eoie_repo_state_1 () = Note ("EOIE-REPO-STATE", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:25Z", "lane-a", "08:25 lane-a: spec coverage map: cases 12,19,23,28,31,32 = 1,371 recorded calls, all red; today's checkpoint metrics (lane-a\\checkpoint\\metrics.ps1) needed git log numstat + ls-files + hashes = 4 calls per repo, a REPO-STATE program.")
inl note_of_eoie_repo_state_2 () = Note ("EOIE-REPO-STATE", 2u32, "2026-10-15T10:50Z", "main-thread", "06:50 groom: evidence from tonight: the pre-commit checks (changed/untracked files per repo, CRLF scan, added-comment scan, tracked .livemd/.ps1 counts) were all hand-written git+pwsh. These are this verb's cases.")
inl note_of_eoie_repo_state_3 () = Note ("EOIE-REPO-STATE", 3u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night use case: the CI state of 7 repos took about 10 separate git and gh calls (latest runs per repo, failed first, the failing step and its error lines); add a CI dimension next to spec case 23.")
inl note_of_eoie_repo_state_4 () = Note ("EOIE-REPO-STATE", 4u32, "2026-10-18T19:53Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 15:53 landed: crate eoie_repo_state, eoie repo state <root>... runs git status --porcelain=v2 --branch and log -1 once per root; typed entry_kind union and change_counts record parse porcelain v2 (renames report the new path, paths keep spaces), per-area tally over two path levels, sorted by change count, top 12 shown with a hidden-count line; e2e on eoie, spiral and x; Spiral tests 2/2")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_1 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 1u32, "2026-10-14T11:50Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-14 07:50 R3 mega roots: outputs identical with instrumentation; W/S 1.00 on all 5; peval only 28-672 ms of 2.5-8.2 s compiles, so parse/typecheck/codegen dominate (D16.4); apps/spiral R3 running")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_2 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 2u32, "2026-10-14T11:52Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-14 07:52 R3 apps/spiral: W 58.0 s, S 20.7 s, W/S 2.80, simulated 2.76x at 8 workers; span = root body 8.6 s + method#639 7.3 s + method#283 4.7 s, so D1 caps near 2.8x; intra-body parallelism is the proposed next decision (after R4)")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_3 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 3u32, "2026-10-14T13:34Z", "main-thread", "09:34 R3 scaling corpus generated (job tmp/hopacsota-p0/r3_scaling_corpus.ps1: N independent modules x 6 join-point levels, main calls each). Plain single-flight Release compile: N=10 3.0 s, N=100 4.8 s (701 C functions), N=1000 stack overflow. Cause: the typechecker recurses term' -> match_clause once per sequential let and runs on a Hopac worker stack, overflowing between 1000 and 2000 lets in one body (2000 dies about 1540 frames deep). Fixed in source (inferOnLargeStack, shared WDiff section, next pack). The W/S scaling measurement for N=1000 waits for that build.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_4 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 4u32, "2026-10-14T16:06Z", "main-thread", "12:06 R4 suite gate (R4 DLL in the night cache, run from a copied apps/compiler/tmp tree so it cannot touch the shared samples): -Suite all compile-only under dfs, bfs, random:11, random:23 and random:37. All 4098 rows have identical compile status and residual hash across the 5 policies (0 differ). Each policy's run has the same 3582 ok and 516 error; 53 rows fail only in the copied tree (package paths), identically under every policy. Caveat: the suite runs did not set SPIRAL_R4_REPORT, so deferral counts come from targeted runs. On the 5 mega roots every policy deferred 24 methods (max queue 24; 0 restarts, 0 validating callers, 0 stack stops) with identical output, but 3 mega roots compile to a trivial program, so the strong check is apps/spiral (1656 specializations), now running under dfs/bfs/random:11 with the report on.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_5 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 5u32, "2026-10-14T16:09Z", "main-thread", "12:09 R4 decided on apps/spiral, with SPIRAL_R4_REPORT on. Every policy defers 636 methods and 579 closures (max queue 1215 under bfs/random; 0 restarts, 0 stack stops). The three outputs differ only in lines 3-60, the global type declaration header (55/58 lines, same multiset of lines); all 18,100 lines of bodies and names after it are byte-identical. So the only order dependence is the order of globals, which is D6 (depth-first merge of globals), and no other cause appears. The PLAN.md scoreboard has the R3/R4 rows and notes. Next: D6 merge in the R4 copy, then 0 differing lines on apps/spiral.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_6 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 6u32, "2026-10-14T16:35Z", "main-thread", "12:35 D6 merge in the R4 copy (each deferred body collects its globals in its own list, a marker records the call position, depth-first flatten after the drain keeps first occurrences): apps/spiral peval globals now match DFS, but the outputs still differ (dfs 18,180 lines vs bfs/random 18,181). The rest is codegen-side. (a) A second globals block that codegen emits (after the UTF-8 helpers) comes out in a different order, so codegen adds its own globals while walking residual bodies in an order that depends on evaluation order (likely join-point dictionary insertion order). (b) type Box<'T> appears in both blocks under bfs, so codegen's dedup set misses the merged entry. Next: find codegen's global' sources and its body walk order, and order codegen by canonical method key (a D7-style rule) before claiming 0 lines.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_7 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 7u32, "2026-10-14T16:35Z", "main-thread", "12:35 hypothesis for the remaining diff (unverified): a memoized join-point body's globals go to whichever globals list was current when it was first evaluated. BackendSwitch validation evaluates the other backends' arms into a throwaway statement list (and possibly a throwaway globals list), and the policies reach validation from different first callers (validating callers dfs 899, bfs 604). So which bodies first run inside validation, and lose their globals to the throwaway or emit them later through codegen, depends on order. If confirmed, the rule is to give each body its globals once, independent of the first caller's context (record per body and merge at its canonical position), and it would also be a latent single-flight dependence. Check: count globals added while RustGapTrace.validating > 0, per policy.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_8 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 8u32, "2026-10-14T18:26Z", "main-thread", "14:26 refuted the 13:0x hypothesis: single-flight's BackendSwitch validation env (spiral_compiler.fs ~163482) replaces seq, cse, backend and the tag counter but keeps s.globals, so validation-time globals reach the real list under every policy. The remaining R4+D6 difference on apps/spiral is narrower: the header still places clap_Command and std_string_String later under bfs, and type Box appears twice. Candidates: a globals path that bypasses peval's global' (codegen's TyOp(Global) arm appends to the same env.globals list, so its position depends on codegen walk order), or a body whose marker lands in a list that is not the one its first DFS caller used. Next: tag each global with its source (peval global', codegen) in the R4 copy and diff per source.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_9 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 9u32, "2026-10-14T19:59Z", "main-thread", "15:59 pinned with the peval-globals dump (R4 + D6 copy, apps/spiral): dfs and bfs hold the SAME 60 globals in a different order (e.g. clap_Command at 3 under dfs and 10 under bfs), so the remaining difference starts in peval, not codegen. Mechanism: a memoized join-point body runs at its first EVALUATION-time caller. Under dfs that is the first caller in depth-first order; under bfs a non-deferred caller can reach the key first, and the body's globals land at that caller's position. Refined D6 rule for the plan: globals belong to the body (its join-point key), not to the caller that happened to evaluate it. Every call site, cache hits included, records a reference marker; the merge expands a key's globals at its first reference in depth-first order and skips later references. The R4 copy needs per-key global lists plus reference markers on memo hits; that is the next experiment.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_10 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 10u32, "2026-10-14T21:21Z", "main-thread", "17:21 key-level D6 tried in the R4 copy: per-key global lists, a marker at the first evaluation and at every memo hit (closure true and method Some ret_ty), expansion at the first depth-first reference. Result on apps/spiral: dfs peval globals unchanged (60 lines, single-flight order), but bfs/random still order them differently in the same places (clap_Command at 3 vs 10), and the dfs OUTPUT changed: type Box now appears twice (line 8 from peval, line 73 from codegen). So (1) the misplaced globals do not come from join-point memo order alone; the next suspect is globals emitted by inline (inl) code inside deferred bodies, which carry no key; (2) the flattened list somehow defeats codegen's dedup (codegen re-adds Box), possibly a marker or near-identical string left behind. Both are open; scripts in job tmp/hopacsota-p0 (r4_deferred.ps1 has the key-level edits; the dump is SPIRAL_R4_GLOBALS_DUMP). Stopping R4 for today.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_11 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 11u32, "2026-10-14T21:52Z", "main-thread", "17:52 mechanism for the duplicate 'type Box': peval's EOp Global arm (~164536) calls global' (adds to s.globals for the matching backend) AND always leaves TyOp(Global) in the residual; codegen's TyOp(Global) arm re-adds it unless its dedup HashSet (seeded from env.globals at codegen start) already holds the string. Under key-level D6 the flattened list shows Box yet codegen re-adds it, so codegen's seed and the flattened list diverge. Next session: dump codegen's seed set and the residual TyOp(Global) strings to find the mismatch.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_12 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 12u32, "2026-10-15T01:15Z", "main-thread", "21:15 NEXT SESSION #3 (P0): close D6. Dump codegen's dedup seed set against the residual TyOp(Global) strings, and add globals from inlined code to the per-key merge (scripts in job tmp/hopacsota-p0). Gate: apps/spiral byte-identical under dfs/bfs/random. Then R3 W/S for N=1000 (now compiles) and close Phase 0.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_13 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 13u32, "2026-10-15T03:25Z", "main-thread", "23:25 D6: the extra 'type Box' in R4's dfs output (key-level merge) is a stale GlobalsIndex, not a codegen dedup bug. Flatten clears and refills the root globals list, but the per-list membership set (ConditionalWeakTable) keeps the old contents, so codegen-time peval (ty_to_data/nominal_apply on the root env) does not see the key-list globals and re-appends them after the codegen helpers. Installed DLL: one Box at line 8. Fix in the scratch r4_deferred.ps1: Flatten refreshes the index. R4b build queued to re-measure dfs/bfs/random:11 on apps/spiral. Rule for the real D6: any merge that rewrites a globals list must rebuild its GlobalsIndex.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_14 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 14u32, "2026-10-15T03:37Z", "main-thread", "23:37 D6 stale-index fix measured (R4b, apps/spiral F#): dfs is now line-for-line identical to the installed compiler (18,180 lines, 0 differ; the duplicate 'type Box' is gone). bfs differs in 44 lines and random:11 in 55 (were 55 and 58), all in the globals header (lines 4-54, same multiset). Example: clap_Command is 4th under dfs and 11th under bfs. Next: a pre-merge tree dump (SPIRAL_R4_TREE_DUMP, list/index/item per globals list; staged in r4_deferred.ps1 as core-r4c.fs) to see which list owns each moved global under each policy. Builds after the pack-1f bless.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_15 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 15u32, "2026-10-15T04:06Z", "main-thread", "00:06 D6 tree dump (R4c, SPIRAL_R4_TREE_DUMP; scripts tmp/hopacsota-p0/tree_paths.ps1): under dfs, 'type clap_Command = class end' sits in the body list of the first app method (key-1), between Ref and clap_Arg. Under bfs the same method's deferred body (key-2 > globals-5) does not contain it. Instead the caller's own list (key-0 body, globals-1) emits it right after the key-2 marker, i.e. after the deferred call returned. These stubs come from nominal bodies (lib backend.spi rust_type -> fsharp_global inside a TTerm), evaluated when the nominal type is resolved and memoized per type. So the emission goes to whichever list resolves the type first in time: under bfs that is the caller, which uses the returned annotated type before the body runs. D6 rule extension: type-level memoized evaluation (nominal resolution / TTerm) must be referenced like a join-point key: a per-type list on first resolution and a marker on every later resolution, expanded at its first depth-first reference. Next: find the nominal resolution memo in single-flight peval (term_real_nominal 162683 is called from ty's TTerm arm 162845) and add type-key markers in the R4 copy.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_16 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 16u32, "2026-10-15T04:07Z", "main-thread", "00:07 correction to the previous note: single-flight's nominal_type_apply (162714) has no memo; it re-evaluates the nominal body (and so its TTerm/fsharp_global) on every resolution, and global' dedups per list. So 'memoized per type' is unverified. What is verified: under bfs the deferred body's list lacks the stub while the caller's list has it after the call. Remaining candidates: the body never resolves that nominal itself (under dfs it got it through a nested call whose annotation is resolved by the caller), or a join-point memo hit without a recorded marker. Next step: an R4 hook that logs (policy, current list, R4 frame stack) whenever global' adds a watched string, instead of more reading.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_17 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 17u32, "2026-10-15T04:36Z", "main-thread", "00:36 D6 found the memo: the type join point cache (join_point_type, single-flight peval ~162759). It evaluates a type join point's body once, so nominal stubs from rust_type/fsharp_global inside it go into the first evaluator's list in time, and a memo hit records nothing (the watch hook confirmed one global' call per run for clap_Command). R4e gives type join points a key list on first evaluation and a marker on every hit, and key markers are ignored once the session closes (codegen-time peval). apps/spiral F# vs installed: dfs 0 lines differ, bfs 13 (was 44; one moved line, std_borrow_Cow), random:11 20 (was 55; Ref, Vec, std_borrow_Cow). Watching std_borrow_Cow next. D6 rule: every memo whose miss can emit globals (method, closure, type join point, and any other found this way) needs key lists plus hit markers.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_18 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 18u32, "2026-10-15T05:41Z", "main-thread", "01:41 D6 lead (R4g, type keys labeled by argument types). The last bfs move is std_borrow_Cow. dfs: its stub comes from type join point [str] (Cow<str>) under run > normalize_path > replace_regex. bfs: the same [str] key under replace_regex has an EMPTY list, and the stub is emitted by [slice u8] under execute_with_options. Hypothesis: the join_point_type memo key has no backend in it. If the [str] body was first evaluated while validating another backend's BackendSwitch arm (bfs validating callers 604 vs dfs 899), fsharp_global's Fsharp arm is not current there, so the memoized evaluation emits no stub. If true, single-flight can drop a stub entirely when a type join point is only ever evaluated first under validation. R4h (labels add backend and validating depth) staged as core-r4h.fs; runs after the pack-1g bless.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_19 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 19u32, "2026-10-15T06:25Z", "main-thread", "02:25 R4h result (type keys labeled with backend and validating depth): the stub-bearing type join point is first evaluated during BackendSwitch validation of another backend's arm. dfs: type@Rust/v1[str] under replace_regex; bfs: type@Gleam/v1[slice u8] under execute_with_options. Validating a non-current arm runs fsharp_global's Fsharp arm, whose global goes into the real globals list. The (backend, closure) validation cache backend_switch_validated is a fourth memo with no hit markers, so in bfs the later [str] evaluation under replace_regex emits nothing. R4i gives backend_switch_validated key lists and hit markers; building. Side finding (lib, not D6): apps/spiral's F# output starts with two Rust lines (thread_local!/#[test]) from lib/spiral/rust/testing.spi run_tests', whose global calls are not behind a Rust backend switch. Same in the installed compiler's output.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_20 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 20u32, "2026-10-15T06:53Z", "main-thread", "02:53 D6 CLOSED for the R4 deferred evaluator. R4i keys the four memos that can emit globals: method, closure and type join points, plus backend_switch_validated, each with a list per key and hit markers. The merge rebuilds the GlobalsIndex, and markers are ignored after the session closes. Results: apps/spiral F# is byte-identical under dfs, bfs and random:11 (EBE4D894C6FB, 18,180 lines) and equal to the installed compiler. Full suite (4,143 rows, copied tree): dfs = bfs = random:11 on every row (compile + residual). dfs vs the installed pack-1g bless differs only in the 53 known copied-tree package-path rows (ok->error); every other row matches. Scoreboard in lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (2026-10-15 entry). Scripts: tmp/hopacsota-p0/r4_deferred.ps1 (core-r4i.fs), tree_paths.ps1. Next for hopacsota: carry the D6 keyed merge (four memo kinds) into the real parallel design (D16), and file the lib run_tests' Rust-globals leak separately.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_21 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 21u32, "2026-10-15T09:49Z", "main-thread", "05:49 NEXT SESSION #2: D6 is proven in the R4 copy. Write the hopacsota phase-1 design that carries the keyed merge (four memo kinds, index rebuild, inert markers after close) into D16's parallel evaluator, and check that the R4 counters for D3's relative context (1,203 relative-trace bodies, 0 restarts) still hold.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_22 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 22u32, "2026-10-15T11:22Z", "main-thread", "07:22 phase 0 gate recorded in PLAN.md (Phase 1 starting point). R1/R2 remain the open parts of this item.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_23 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 23u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: R3 instrumentation patch no longer applies (its PartEval anchor moved behind PartEvalSeams in pack-1v); re-home R3 into PartEvalSeamsHopacsota, which already sees every deferred body.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_24 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 24u32, "2026-10-19T12:17Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:17 lap 1 grain: closed: PLAN.md scoreboard has all four Phase 0 gates (R1 and R2 2026-10-14 00:5x, R3 07:52, R4 12:08) and Phase 1 Gate 1 passed 2026-10-16 11:18, so the 10-15 note that R1/R2 remain open is stale; the R3/R4 scripts moved out of job tmp into spiral/lab/HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH (9 scripts, LF; run outputs stay in job tmp); re-homing the R3 instrumentation into PartEvalSeamsHopacsota belongs to HOPACSOTA-P3 (measured granularity cutoff) Next: -")
inl note_of_hopacsota_research_25 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", 25u32, "2026-10-22T04:05Z", "main", "00:05 lab drained: the 9 R3/R4 instruments are promoted into the lane's tracked folder apps/compiler/tmp/lanes/hopacsota/research/ (uncommitted for the user), beside hopac-probes; their results are PLAN.md's Phase 0 scoreboard (R1-R4). One change: r3_scaling_corpus.ps1 and r3_scaling_time.ps1 now generate their corpus under spiral-bin/hopacsota-r3-scaling instead of beside the script, so runs never write into the tree. The R3 instrumentation re-home stays with HOPACSOTA-P3. Removed spiral/lab/HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH (9 files).")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_rename_id_1 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-RENAME-ID", 1u32, "2026-10-14T13:38Z", "lane-b", "renew-strict-evidence.ps1 run 08:27-09:37 (through the gate): build -Test ok, cold builds a=b identical, 145 owners replayed with 0 hard failures, but the cold budget failed under today's load (max owner 68 s, global gate 25 s) and the script retried at 1 chain; stopped it to free gate slot 1, state/ restored to HEAD; rerun on a quiet machine (evening)")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_rename_id_2 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-RENAME-ID", 2u32, "2026-10-14T22:18Z", "lane-b", "renewal retry 18:01 (1 chain, after the pack-1e install and the eoie regeneration): stopped at build.ps1 -Test -CompilerContracts, one eoie-contracts lib test (reversible_self_patch_fixture_roundtrips...) hit its 40 s command timeout with the CPU at 100% (other lane's compiler build); no state/ change; rerun on a quiet machine")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_rename_id_3 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-RENAME-ID", 3u32, "2026-10-14T23:24Z", "lane-b", "renewal attempt 3 (18:58, 1 chain) failed the cold budget too: max owner 22,459 ms (other owners slowest this time: noisy machine), so stopped for tonight with state/ at HEAD; next: split src/bundle_retention_domain/main.spi (main's decision), then renew on a quiet machine")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_rename_id_4 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-RENAME-ID", 4u32, "2026-10-14T23:33Z", "lane-b", "18:58 detail: bundle_retention was 4.3 s; eoie_agile_state 18.6 s, archive_contracts 22.5 s, patch_grammar 21.9 s, patch_mutation 19.2 s went over 15 s (median 4.3 s). Owner time follows load; renew on a quiet machine")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_rename_id_5 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-RENAME-ID", 5u32, "2026-10-15T10:48Z", "main-thread", "06:48 groom: verified on eoie.exe of 10-15: agile rename <root> <old> <new> works (scratch root: T-ONE -> T-TWO, reports deps_rewritten and title mentions). Done.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_1 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:39Z", "main-thread", "08:39 compiled lane 3's 7 drafted frontier_hopacsota_* fixtures (job tmp/hopacsota-fixtures) with the installed single-flight Release DLL. 6 match their predictions: globals_order emits m1 a1 c1 a2 b1 m2 and exits 0; validation_global emits g1, then nested validation global once, then g2; mutual_pending and pending_type_join_point exit 0; if_depth_across_fork raises EJP0040; two_errors reports 'first body fails' at 12:10. recursion_unannotated is wrong: it compiles and exits 0, and so does a variant with the recursive call in the then branch. EJoinPoint' annot (163017) comes from the prepass's inferred type, so a plain let rec reaches peval as Some. The error at 163000 needs a join point whose type the prepass leaves None. Next: find that shape (an explicit join, or a polymorphic body) before blessing the fixture.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_2 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 2u32, "2026-10-14T12:40Z", "main-thread", "08:40 explicit 'inl rec count (n : i32) = join if ...' also compiles, with the recursive call in either branch, so the typechecker fills the join's annotation too (RawAnnot around RawJoinPoint, 55283). An annot=None join point may be unreachable from source; if so the 163000 arm is dead code for hopacsota D4, and the fixture should instead pin 'inferred annotation lets pending recursion return without waiting'. Scratch variants are in job tmp/hopacsota-fixtures/scratch_join_*.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_3 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 3u32, "2026-10-14T13:01Z", "main-thread", "09:01 settled: the typechecker's fill pass wraps every RawJoinPoint as RawAnnot(r, RawJoinPoint(...), annot r x) (spiral_compiler.fs 50402, and 52724 on the other side). Backend-switch join points (join_point_backend, 44452) take the same path, so the prepass always builds EJoinPoint' with Some annotation and peval's 'Recursive join points must be annotated' arm (163000) is unreachable from type-checked source. For hopacsota D4: keep that case as a defensive compiler error, not a scheduled waiter rule. Replace frontier_hopacsota_recursion_unannotated with a fixture where pending recursion returns its inferred type without waiting (both of lane 3's orderings already compile: exit 0).")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_4 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 4u32, "2026-10-15T10:51Z", "main-thread", "06:51 groom: input from 10-15: the merge rules P1 must carry are now concrete (four memo kinds with key lists and hit markers, index rebuild after merge, inert markers after close; R4 copy tmp/hopacsota-p0/r4_deferred.ps1). Ready to start after the design note.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_5 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 5u32, "2026-10-15T11:22Z", "main-thread", "07:22 main: phase-1 design note written into lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (Phase 1 starting point): R4's gate is met and its keyed merge carries over unchanged (four global-emitting memos, references on hits, depth-first expansion, GlobalsIndex rebuild, inert after close); frontier_hopacsota_globals_order now names the two concrete cases R4 found. Next grain: the -Mode hopacsota plumbing in build/test/probe/env/projection-hash.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_6 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 6u32, "2026-10-15T14:29Z", "main-thread", "10:29 main: Phase 1 step 1 done (plumbing). -Mode hopacsota (alias hs) in env.ps1 ConvertTo-SpiralMode, build.ps1, test.ps1 (a candidate like gpt5parallel: broken rows report 'missing', UNEXPECTED-OUTPUT not fatal, -Bless refused), probe.ps1, fast-tier.ps1 (run prefix hopacsota-), test-rust-exports.ps1, projection-hash.ps1. Core fsproj defines SPIRAL_CORE_HOPACSOTA; host defines SPIRAL_CORE_SINGLE_FLIGHT plus SPIRAL_CORE_HOPACSOTA (the host sees single-flight's API). Gate check: projection-hash gives hopacsota = single-flight (cad3e1792ab19b4a, 28,150 lines). Next: a first -Mode hopacsota build after the current packs, then hopacsota-lint.ps1 (G2) and the size budget (G1), then the deferred worklist from R4i.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_7 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 7u32, "2026-10-15T14:30Z", "main-thread", "10:30 main: G1/G2 gate script added: scripts/hopacsota-lint.ps1 (-Size: layer <= 5,934 lines, no section > 1,000; -Banned: the PLAN's G2 list incl. the D2 identifiers replay/record/resume/snapshot/ledger, allowlist in-script, empty). It scans only #if SPIRAL_CORE_HOPACSOTA sides. build.ps1 -Mode hopacsota runs it and fails on a violation. Tree: 0 layer lines, 0 hits. A probe with a ConcurrentDictionary and a replayStore identifier reports both and exits 1.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_8 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 8u32, "2026-10-15T15:18Z", "main-thread", "11:18 design gap before the worklist step: D10 wants seams as hooks whose single-flight implementation is the current code moved unchanged, and also single-flight's projection hash unchanged (G6). Moving the seam code changes the call-site text in single-flight's PartEval side, so the hash cannot stay equal literally. Options: (a) G6 compares projections modulo the named seam call sites (projection-hash.ps1 learns a seam list), or (b) seams stay inline and hopacsota wraps them in a Hopacsota layer section that shadows the enclosing function. Needs a decision before the R4i worklist moves into a layer; recorded instead of improvised.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_9 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 9u32, "2026-10-15T15:49Z", "main-thread", "11:49 D10/G6 decided (main, autonomous): seams become calls into a PartEvalSeams module defined in a hopacsota layer pair before PartEval (single-flight side = the moved code, hopacsota side = the deferred worklist from R4i). G6 changes from 'projection hash unchanged' to (1) single-flight's oracle unchanged (review identical) and (2) single-flight's projection diff contains only lines that call PartEvalSeams. projection-hash.ps1 gets a -Seams check and pair-drift.ps1 accepts a one-sided PartEval change only when every changed line is a PartEvalSeams call. Next: implement those two checks, then move the first seam (type join point memo).")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_10 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 10u32, "2026-10-15T15:55Z", "main-thread", "11:55 G6 seam checks implemented: pair-drift.ps1 now allows a one-sided single-flight change when every added code line calls PartEvalSeams (probe repo: seam edit passes, non-seam edit fails); projection-hash.ps1 -Seams [-Base HEAD] compares single-flight's projection to the base and fails unless every added line is a PartEvalSeams call (on today's tree it correctly flags the uncommitted pack changes). env.ps1 Get-SpiralCoreProjection takes an optional -Source. First -Mode hopacsota build: 228 s, G1 0 lines, G2 0 hits. Next: the PartEvalSeams pair and the first seam (type join point memo), in a session after today's packs are committed (the -Seams base must be clean).")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_11 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 11u32, "2026-10-16T13:53Z", "main-thread", "09:53 main: seams step built (job tmp/hopacsota-p1/seams.ps1, on a copy of the pack-1u tree): PartEvalSeams pair before PartEval; single-flight side = inline no-ops (start/defer/root/key_hit/key_body), hopacsota side = R4's deferral + keyed merge (policy SPIRAL_HOPACSOTA_POLICY inline|dfs|bfs|random:N) plus D4's error rule (failures kept as markers in the body's list, the first on the depth-first walk is raised); 9 single-flight call sites. G1 128 lines, G2 0 hits, G6 structural: 14 added projection lines, all PartEvalSeams calls or ')'. Tooling for G6: projection-hash -BaseFile, -w diff, PartEvalSeams section stripped; Get-SpiralCoreProjection resolves SPIRAL_CORE_HOPACSOTA; pair-drift -w (decision change in PLAN.md). Fixtures added: frontier_hopacsota_recursion_inferred, mutual_pending, globals_order (m1 a1 c1 a2 b1 m2), two_errors (first body fails; ExpectedErrors entry); single-flight outcomes match the drafts' predictions. globals_order does not yet cover R4's two concrete cases (nominal stub under validation, type join point hit by a deferred body); apps/spiral covers them. Running: G3 compile-only suites single-flight (G6 semantic vs bless 092123) + hopacsota inline/dfs/bfs/random:11/23/37.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_12 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 12u32, "2026-10-16T15:29Z", "main-thread", "11:29 main: GATE 1 MET (numbers in PLAN.md scoreboard). G1 131 lines, G2 0; -Suite all compile-only (6,758 rows): single-flight with seams = pack-1u oracle 092123 on every compile/residual/error cell (G6 semantic); hopacsota inline/dfs/bfs/random:11/23/37 each 0 differing cells (runs hopacsota-20261016-105126..110811); apps/spiral F# (963,180 B) and Rust (1,590,762 B) byte-identical under all 7; inline A/B (best of 3, interleaved) sum 0.996x, median 1.007x, mega roots <= 1.031x. v3 adds D4's first-error rule (two_errors failed random:23 without it) and compile-time prints as ordered markers (PrintStatic order differed under bfs/random before). Landed in the tree as pack-1v (seams.ps1 has a guard that every call-site edit sits on single-flight's PartEval side: the first print anchor had matched the gpt5parallel side). Left in Phase 1's structure: D3 Owner/Waiter capability, D8 phantom keys, globals_order pinning R4's two cases.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_13 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 13u32, "2026-10-16T15:59Z", "main-thread", "11:59 main: pack-1v installed both modes (11:22/11:28) and blessed: single-flight-20261016-112838, 6,758 rows, DISAGREE 0, 0 differing cells against pack-1u's 092123; the 16 extra rows are the 4 frontier_hopacsota fixtures on Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi (Rust and Delphi agree with C; two_errors is an error row on all four). The seams are in the tree and installed; single-flight output unchanged.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_14 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 14u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: closing: Gate 1 met 10-16 11:29 and pack-1v installed and blessed 11:59 (seams in the tree, single-flight output unchanged); the 80 percent was stale.")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_body_1 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-BODY", 1u32, "2026-10-14T08:49Z", "lane 2", "first real note: written by eoie agile note itself (lane 2 build from src/target/debug); notes are Note items (id, seq, UTC instant, author, text) after the task's Task/Planning lines, the task_note union is added on first use, agile show prints them under the title and --json as a notes array")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_body_2 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-BODY", 2u32, "2026-10-14T08:56Z", "lane 2", "lane 2 done (uncommitted, eoie repo): eoie agile note <root> <id> <text> [--as <author>] and agile notes from-title <root> <id>, granular Spiral, no new rust_global: package agile_note_model (Note rows, task_note schema added on first use, insertion after the task's Task/Planning/Note lines, unescape, UTC civil-date stamp, guarded write that re-reads the file and refuses with 'state/agile.spi changed since it was read'), crates agile_task_notes (637 generated lines), agile_note_listing (418, notes text and JSON for show), agile_title_tails (406, the '; ' split with yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm / HH:mm stamps carried forward), agile_title_notes (776); agile show prints 'notes (N)' and '<at>  <author>  <text>' lines under the title, --json adds a notes array of {at, author, text}; routed in eoie_agile_mutation, registered in command_spec_domain, README updated; every crate under the 1000-line gate; tree .rs byte-identical to dev.ps1's staged regeneration")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_body_3 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-BODY", 3u32, "2026-10-14T08:56Z", "lane 2", "proof: on a copy of this backlog two notes (quotes and a backslash round-trip), from-title on HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH moved 15 notes (title 2,099 -> 108 bytes), agile check build_attested=2 on the copy; tests src/eoie_contracts/tests/agile_note_receipts.rs 4/4 (whole receipt lines, show text and JSON, rejections leave state byte-identical, concurrent writer), with agile_receipts and proxy_receipts 10/10 against src/target/debug/eoie.exe; dev.ps1 on the 10 packages: 10/10 emitted, cargo check ok, package tests ok except eoie-contracts lib expired_lease_blocks_first_mutation_but_keeps_wrap_surface (failed once under load at 232 s; passes alone with the same dev-validation binary and with the deployed one); real backlog: these notes, agile check build_attested=2; left: deploy the new eoie.exe (the deployed one does not print notes), renew owner growth and strict evidence (compiler-contracts/renew-strict-evidence.ps1), migrate long titles with notes from-title when their lanes are idle")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_body_4 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-BODY", 4u32, "2026-10-14T09:20Z", "lane 2", "review round: the after-read test pause now writes state/agile.spi.paused so the concurrent-writer test waits for the marker instead of a fixed sleep; new test an_expired_lease_blocks_note_from_title_and_rename_alike (expired prompt.spi lease, no lease policy): note, notes from-title and rename are all refused with 'lease authority blocked mutating effect' and leave the state byte-identical, so the from-title root position does not bypass the lease; agile_note_receipts 5/5; eoie-contracts lib suite 8/8 (7 ignored) in the tree against the deployed eoie.exe (14 s), the new debug build (132 s) and dev.ps1's dev-validation build (108 s); dev.ps1 -Package <the 10 packages> emitted 10/10 and passed cargo check and every package test except eoie-contracts lib expired_lease_blocks_first_mutation_but_keeps_wrap_surface, which failed in both staged runs (239 s) although the same binaries pass it in the tree: cause not found, next: dev.ps1 -Package eoie-contracts on a clean checkout to see whether it predates this change")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_body_5 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-BODY", 5u32, "2026-10-14T09:24Z", "lane 2", "staged-only lease failure explained: eoie-contracts lib expired_lease_blocks_first_mutation_but_keeps_wrap_surface clears EOIE_LEASE_POLICY but not EOIE_LEASE_ROOT (contracts.rs:158, from contracts_entry/harness.spi), and an inherited EOIE_LEASE_ROOT pointing at a live lease reproduces the failure in the tree with the same dev-validation binary (fails in 0.07 s; passes without it), so it is a pre-existing test fragility of the staged dev workflow, not this change; fix: env_remove(EOIE_LEASE_ROOT) in that test's commands (needs contracts.rs regeneration); topology after this batch: topology_limits_ok=true, cargo_crate_count=134 (was 128), rust_global_site_count=261 (unchanged), largest crate 995 lines (rust_std_fs_mutation); the round-2 edits (pause marker, rename guards) were compiled directly with the same compiler and not yet compared with a staged regeneration")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_body_6 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-BODY", 6u32, "2026-10-14T10:01Z", "lane 2", "deployed: eoie build.ps1 (release 3m33s, schema and source-topology checks) published the repo-root eoie.exe (sha256 DD36D652D7AB.. -> 44897B5C8234..); this deployed binary prints these notes under the title (agile show) and as a 5-entry notes array (--json), and agile check on this backlog passes (build_attested=1); before that eoie dev.ps1 -Package on the 11 affected packages -Publish passed end to end (719 s, 0 owners changed): eoie-contracts lib 8/8 incl. the lease test, agile_note_receipts 6/6, agile_receipts 1/1, proxy_receipts 5/5, batch_completion 2/2; the earlier staged-only lease failure came from contracts.rs being hand-patched in a743a92 without its source contracts_entry/harness.spi, now carried in the source (plus env_remove EOIE_LEASE_ROOT); note the release also contains the other lane's uncommitted proxy_failure_classification/eoie_proxy_edit_contracts edits; not done: compiler-contracts/renew-strict-evidence.ps1 (build.ps1 -Test -CompilerContracts on the whole workspace, cold rebuild of every chain, release-closeout apply), which would take well over the remaining time and bake the other lane's uncommitted edits into evidence: run it after both lanes commit")
